export const bodyHtml = "\n<p>Putting a desk in a bedroom works until it blocks the closet door. The trick is picking the spot before the desk, then choosing a desk that fits the spot instead of the other way around.</p>\n<p>These layouts help you find that spot, check clearance, and keep the bedroom feeling like a bedroom.</p>\n<p><strong>Quick answer:</strong> Tape the desk outline on the floor, then check that you still have about 30 by 48 inches of clear space for the chair, the closet and the door. Favour a narrow desk, a corner, the window wall or a spot at the foot of the bed, and keep the work area visually separate from the pillow side.</p>\n<h2 id=\"where-to-put-it\">Where to put the desk</h2>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Spot</th><th>Works well when</th><th>Watch out for</th></tr></thead><tbody>\n<tr><td>Window wall</td><td>You want daylight</td><td>Glare on the screen</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Corner</td><td>The corner is free of doors</td><td>Chair swing against walls</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Foot of the bed</td><td>The room is long</td><td>Blocks walking space</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Closet niche</td><td>The closet is shallow</td><td>Heat and ventilation</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Behind a door</td><td>The door opens fully</td><td>Chair against the door</td></tr>\n</tbody></table></div><p>Our <a href=\"/guide/best-desks-for-bedrooms\">best desks for bedrooms</a> and <a href=\"/guide/best-small-desks\">small desk picks</a> compare sizes, and the <a href=\"/guide/small-desk-setup\">small desk setup guide</a> has more layout ideas.</p>\n<h2 id=\"clearance\">Clearance and measuring</h2>\n<p>Use painter's tape for the desk and a second outline for the chair pulled out. Walk the path to the bed, the closet and the door. If anything snags, move the outline. One dorm furniture guide gives 30 by 48 inches of clear floor at a desk as a useful target.</p>\n<h2 id=\"separating-work-and-sleep\">Separating work from sleep</h2>\n<p>A small screen, a rug under the desk or a shelf between the desk and the bed gives a visual break. Facing away from the bed when you work helps you close the day. Dim the lamp in the evening.</p>\n<h2 id=\"storage-and-clutter\">Storage and clutter</h2>\n<p>Use wall space and under-bed bins for items you do not use daily. Our <a href=\"/guide/how-to-organize-a-small-desk\">small desk organising guide</a> and <a href=\"/guide/best-desk-hutches-for-small-desks\">small desk hutches</a> suggest ways to add storage without a bigger footprint.</p>\n<h2 id=\"light-and-noise\">Light, noise and shared walls</h2>\n<p>A warm desk lamp avoids lighting the whole room. Keyboard noise carries through shared walls, so a soft desk mat helps. See <a href=\"/guide/best-desk-pads-for-small-desks\">desk pads for small desks</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"faq\">Frequently asked questions</h2>\n<h3>How do I set up a desk in a small bedroom?</h3>\n<p>Choose the spot first, tape the outline, check chair and door clearance, then pick a desk that fits.</p>\n<h3>Where is the best place for a desk in a small bedroom?</h3>\n<p>Often the window wall or a corner. Choose the one that does not block the closet or door.</p>\n<h3>How much space does a bedroom desk need?</h3>\n<p>Plan the desk footprint plus about 30 by 48 inches of clear floor for the chair.</p>\n<h3>How do I keep my bedroom from feeling like an office?</h3>\n<p>Use a rug, shelf or screen to separate zones, face away from the bed, and clear the desk at night.</p>\n<h3>What size desk fits a small bedroom?</h3>\n<p>A narrow desk about 40 to 48 inches wide fits most rooms, and wall-mounted or corner models fit tighter ones.</p>\n<h3>Can I use a desk in front of a window?</h3>\n<p>Yes, but angle the monitor to avoid glare and use a blind in the afternoon.</p>\n<h2 id=\"sources-and-scope\">Sources and scope</h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"https://unfnshed.com/blogs/news/desk-for-dorm-room\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Unfnshed dorm desk guide</a>: clear floor space around a desk</li><li><a href=\"https://www.csuci.edu/publicsafety/ehs/200320-ci-workstation-setup-checklist.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">CSU Channel Islands workstation checklist</a>: a posture checklist to test the spot</li><li><a href=\"https://www.aut.ac.nz/__data/assets/pdf_file/0004/782680/Setting-up-your-workstation-tip-sheet.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">AUT workstation tip sheet</a>: chair and reach checks before settling on a place</li></ul>\n<p>Clearance numbers are planning guidance, not a building code. Check your lease and local safety rules before blocking a window or exit.</p>";
